IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-definitions-products`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 12, Division 1 (ss 196 to 204): prohibited conduct in capital markets products. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- How to read an answer. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (yes), JUST FALSE (the TEXT says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Each branch that says no carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, each branch that says "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- `-- SPLIT-SITE (i)` / `(ii)` marks the branch whose answer the family has left open (NOTES.md, Split sites); `-- MARGINAL-READING (a)` / `(b)` marks a branch
-- resting on one of the two readings left to a lawyer (NOTES.md, Marginal readings). The key in [..] names the Guide line the answer relies on.
-- The Act's own words are used for the inputs; "(as section 3 reads)" inputs take the answer of the keel's `s 3(1)` function (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING).
-- Regulative rules: PARTY ... SHANT, with the party a core `Party` and the act a constructor of the section's own type.

§ `s 196: application of Division 1`

-- src:34183 | 196. This Division applies to —
@ref s 196 (src:34183-34183)
GIVEN
    `this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore (the answer under section 196(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 196(a) answer for this act? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore (the answer under section 196(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 196(b) answer for this act? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196 this Division applies to the act` MEANS
    IF (`this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore (the answer under section 196(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore (the answer under section 196(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division applies to"

-- src:34185 | (a) acts occurring within Singapore in relation to —
-- src:34187 | (i) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34188 | any corporation, whether formed or carrying on
-- src:34189 | business in Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:34191 | (ii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34192 | any business trust;
-- src:34194 | (iii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:34195 | listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market
-- src:34196 | in Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:34198 | (iv) units in a collective investment scheme listed for
-- src:34199 | quotation or quoted on an organised market in
-- src:34200 | Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:34202 | (v) derivatives contracts, whether traded in Singapore or
-- src:34203 | elsewhere;
-- src:34205 | (vi) spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of
-- src:34206 | leveraged foreign exchange trading, whether traded
-- src:34207 | in Singapore or elsewhere; or
-- src:34209 | (vii) any other capital markets products, whether traded in
-- src:34210 | Singapore or elsewhere; and
@ref s 196(a) (src:34185-34210)
GIVEN
    `the act occurs within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act occur within Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation, whether formed or carrying on business in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation, whether formed or carrying on business in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to units in a collective investment scheme listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to units in a collective investment scheme listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to derivatives contracts, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to derivatives contracts, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to any other capital markets products, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to any other capital markets products, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(a) this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the act occurs within Singapore` AND (`the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation, whether formed or carrying on business in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to units in a collective investment scheme listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to derivatives contracts, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to any other capital markets products, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division applies to" "acts occurring within Singapore in relation to" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [SCOPE]

-- src:34212 | (b) acts occurring outside Singapore in relation to —
-- src:34214 | (i) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34215 | a corporation that is formed or carrying on business
-- src:34216 | in Singapore;
-- src:34218 | (ii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34219 | a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in
-- src:34224 | Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the
-- src:34225 | business trust in Singapore;
-- src:34227 | (iii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:34228 | listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market
-- src:34229 | in Singapore;
-- src:34231 | (iv) units in a collective investment scheme listed for
-- src:34232 | quotation or quoted on an organised market in
-- src:34233 | Singapore;
-- src:34235 | (v) derivatives contracts traded in Singapore;
-- src:34237 | (vi) spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of
-- src:34238 | leveraged foreign exchange trading that are traded in
-- src:34239 | or accessible from Singapore; or
-- src:34241 | (vii) any other capital markets products that are traded in
-- src:34242 | Singapore.
@ref s 196(b) (src:34212-34242)
GIVEN
    `the act occurs outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act occur outside Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation that is formed or carrying on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation that is formed or carrying on business in Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the business trust in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the business trust in Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore?
    `the act relates to units in a collective investment scheme listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to units in a collective investment scheme listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore?
    `the act relates to derivatives contracts traded in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to derivatives contracts traded in Singapore?
    `the act relates to spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading that are traded in or accessible from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading that are traded in or accessible from Singapore?
    `the act relates to any other capital markets products that are traded in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to any other capital markets products that are traded in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196(b) this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the act occurs outside Singapore` AND (`the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation that is formed or carrying on business in Singapore` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the business trust in Singapore` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` OR `the act relates to units in a collective investment scheme listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` OR `the act relates to derivatives contracts traded in Singapore` OR `the act relates to spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading that are traded in or accessible from Singapore` OR `the act relates to any other capital markets products that are traded in Singapore`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "acts occurring outside Singapore in relation to" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [SCOPE]

§ `s 196A: interpretation of Division 1`

-- src:34248 | 196A. In this Division —
-- src:34250 | (a) “debenture” has the meaning given by section 2(1) and, in
-- src:34251 | relation to a business trust, means any debenture issued by
-- src:34252 | the trustee‑manager of the business trust in its capacity as
-- src:34253 | trustee‑manager of the business trust;
@ref s 196A(a) (src:34248-34253)
GIVEN
    `the instrument is a debenture as section 2(1) defines it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 2(1) "debenture" answer for this instrument? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the debenture is in relation to a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debenture one in relation to a business trust?
    `the debenture was issued by the trustee-manager of the business trust in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the debenture issued by the trustee-manager of the business trust in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(a) the instrument is a debenture for the purposes of this Division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the debenture is in relation to a business trust`
        THEN `the instrument is a debenture as section 2(1) defines it`
        IF `the instrument is a debenture as section 2(1) defines it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 2(1)"
        IF NOT `the debenture was issued by the trustee-manager of the business trust in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a business trust, means any debenture issued by the trustee-manager of the business trust in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust"
        IF `the instrument is a debenture as section 2(1) defines it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer under section 2(1) "debenture" was not given

-- src:34255 | (b) a reference to a securities‑based derivatives contract of a
-- src:34256 | corporation in sections 196(a)(i) and (b)(i), 198, 202 and
-- src:34257 | 203 is to be read as a reference to a securities‑based
-- src:34258 | derivatives contract of which the underlying thing or any of
-- src:34259 | the underlying things are securities of the corporation; and
@ref s 196A(b) (src:34255-34259)
GIVEN
    `the contract is a derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a derivatives contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the underlying thing of the contract (or any one of its underlying things) a security or a securities index?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this contract, or its class of derivatives contracts, as not being a securities-based derivatives contract?
    `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, are securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the underlying thing of the contract (or any one of its underlying things) a security of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(b) the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract of the corporation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2(1) "securities-based derivatives contract" the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract` `the contract is a derivatives contract` `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index` `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the keel's s 2(1) answer is NOTHING
        IF (`s 2(1) "securities-based derivatives contract" the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract` `the contract is a derivatives contract` `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index` `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, are securities of the corporation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be read as a reference to a securities-based derivatives contract of which the underlying thing or any of the underlying things are securities of the corporation"

-- src:34261 | (c) a reference to a securities‑based derivatives contract of a
-- src:34262 | business trust in sections 196(a)(ii) and (b)(ii), 198, 202
-- src:34263 | and 203 is to be read as a reference to a securities‑based
-- src:34264 | derivatives contract of which the underlying thing or any of
-- src:34265 | the underlying things, are securities of the business trust.
@ref s 196A(c) (src:34261-34265)
GIVEN
    `the contract is a derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a derivatives contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the underlying thing of the contract (or any one of its underlying things) a security or a securities index?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this contract, or its class of derivatives contracts, as not being a securities-based derivatives contract?
    `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, are securities of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the underlying thing of the contract (or any one of its underlying things) a security of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(c) the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract of the business trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2(1) "securities-based derivatives contract" the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract` `the contract is a derivatives contract` `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index` `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the keel's s 2(1) answer is NOTHING
        IF (`s 2(1) "securities-based derivatives contract" the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract` `the contract is a derivatives contract` `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index` `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, are securities of the business trust`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be read as a reference to a securities-based derivatives contract of which the underlying thing or any of the underlying things, are securities of the business trust"

§ `s 197: false trading and market rigging transactions`

-- src:34274 | 197.—(1) A person must not do any thing, cause any thing to be
-- src:34275 | done or engage in any course of conduct, if the person’s purpose, or
-- src:34276 | any of the person’s purposes, for doing that thing, causing that thing
-- src:34277 | to be done or engaging in that course of conduct (as the case may be)
-- src:34278 | is to create a false or misleading appearance —
-- src:34280 | (a) of active trading in any capital markets products on an
-- src:34281 | organised market; or
-- src:34283 | (b) with respect to the market for, or the price of, any capital
-- src:34284 | markets products traded on an organised market.
@ref s 197(1) (src:34274-34284)
GIVEN
    `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct?
    `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's purpose, or one of the person's purposes, for it to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market?
    `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's purpose, or one of the person's purposes, for it to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market?
    `the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading is presumed under section 197(3) and the presumption is not rebutted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading presumed under section 197(3), and has the presumption not been rebutted under section 197(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on conduct done to create a false or misleading appearance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not do any thing, cause any thing to be done or engage in any course of conduct" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market` OR `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market` OR `the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading is presumed under section 197(3) and the presumption is not rebutted`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person’s purpose, or any of the person’s purposes" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 197(1) (src:34274-34284)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 to s 203 prohibited act`
`s 197(1) a person must not act for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 197(1) do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person did a thing, caused it to be done or engaged in a course of conduct for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance (section 197(1))"

-- src:34288 | (1A) A person must not do any thing, cause any thing to be done or
-- src:34289 | engage in any course of conduct that creates, or is likely to create, a
-- src:34290 | false or misleading appearance of active trading in any capital
-- src:34291 | markets products on an organised market, or with respect to the
-- src:34292 | market for, or the price of, any capital markets products traded on an
-- src:34293 | organised market, if —
-- src:34295 | (a) the person knows that doing that thing, causing that thing
-- src:34296 | to be done or engaging in that course of conduct (as the
-- src:34297 | case may be) will create, or will be likely to create, that
-- src:34298 | false or misleading appearance; or
-- src:34300 | (b) the person is reckless as to whether doing that thing,
-- src:34301 | causing that thing to be done or engaging in that course of
-- src:34302 | conduct (as the case may be) will create, or will be likely to
-- src:34303 | create, that false or misleading appearance.
@ref s 197(1A) (src:34288-34303)
GIVEN
    `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct?
    `the thing creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market, or with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the thing create, or is it likely to create, a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market, or with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market?
    `the person knows that the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person know that doing the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance?
    `the person is reckless as to whether the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person reckless as to whether doing the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1A) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on conduct that creates a false or misleading appearance knowingly or recklessly` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` AND `the thing creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market, or with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance of active trading" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the person knows that the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance` OR `the person is reckless as to whether the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if" "the person knows that doing that thing" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 197(1A) (src:34288-34303)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 to s 203 prohibited act`
`s 197(1A) a person must not do a thing that creates a false or misleading appearance knowingly or recklessly` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 197(1A) do a thing that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance, knowingly or recklessly`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person did a thing that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance, knowing or reckless that it would (section 197(1A))"

-- src:34307 | (2) A person must not maintain, inflate, depress, or cause
-- src:34308 | fluctuations in, the market price of any capital markets products —
-- src:34310 | (a) by means of any purchase or sale of any capital markets
-- src:34311 | products that does not involve a change in the beneficial
-- src:34312 | ownership of the capital markets products; or
-- src:34314 | (b) by any fictitious transaction or device.
@ref s 197(2) (src:34307-34314)
GIVEN
    `the person maintained, inflated, depressed or caused fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person maintain, inflate, depress or cause fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products?
    `the person did so by a purchase or sale that does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership (the answer under section 197(5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Did the person do so by means of a purchase or sale of capital markets products that does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 197(5), or NOTHING if not known)
    `the person did so by a fictitious transaction or device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person do so by a fictitious transaction or device?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(2) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on maintaining, inflating or depressing the market price` MEANS
    IF `the person maintained, inflated, depressed or caused fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products` AND ((`the person did so by a purchase or sale that does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership (the answer under section 197(5))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person did so by a fictitious transaction or device`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by means of any purchase or sale of any capital markets products that does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

@ref s 197(2) (src:34307-34314)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 to s 203 prohibited act`
`s 197(2) a person must not maintain, inflate or depress the market price by a sale with no change in beneficial ownership or a fictitious transaction` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 197(2) maintain, inflate, depress or cause fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products by a purchase or sale with no change in beneficial ownership, or by a fictitious transaction or device`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person maintained, inflated, depressed or caused fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products by a purchase or sale with no change in beneficial ownership or by a fictitious transaction (section 197(2))"

-- src:34318 | (3) Without limiting subsection (1), it is presumed that a person’s
-- src:34319 | purpose, or one of a person’s purposes, is to create a false or
-- src:34324 | misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products
-- src:34325 | on an organised market if the person —
@ref s 197(3) (src:34318-34325)
GIVEN
    `the presumption arises under paragraph (a) (the answer under section 197(3)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 197(3)(a) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the presumption arises under paragraph (b) (the answer under section 197(3)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 197(3)(b) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the presumption arises under paragraph (c) (the answer under section 197(3)(c))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 197(3)(c) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(3) the person's purpose is presumed to be to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading` MEANS
    IF (`the presumption arises under paragraph (a) (the answer under section 197(3)(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the presumption arises under paragraph (b) (the answer under section 197(3)(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the presumption arises under paragraph (c) (the answer under section 197(3)(c))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting subsection (1)"

-- src:34327 | (a) effects, takes part in, is concerned in or carries out, directly
-- src:34328 | or indirectly, any transaction of purchase or sale of the
-- src:34329 | capital markets products, being a transaction that does not
-- src:34330 | involve any change in the beneficial ownership of the
-- src:34331 | capital markets products;
@ref s 197(3)(a) (src:34327-34331)
GIVEN
    `the person effects, takes part in, is concerned in or carries out, directly or indirectly, a transaction of purchase or sale of the capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person effect, take part in, is the person concerned in or carry out, directly or indirectly, a transaction of purchase or sale of the capital markets products?
    `the transaction does not involve any change in the beneficial ownership (the answer under section 197(5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Does the transaction not involve any change in the beneficial ownership of the capital markets products? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 197(5), or NOTHING if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(3)(a) the person's purpose is presumed by reason of a transaction with no change in beneficial ownership` MEANS
    IF `the person effects, takes part in, is concerned in or carries out, directly or indirectly, a transaction of purchase or sale of the capital markets products` AND (`the transaction does not involve any change in the beneficial ownership (the answer under section 197(5))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting subsection (1)"

-- src:34333 | (b) makes or causes to be made an offer to sell the capital
-- src:34334 | markets products at a specified price, where the person has
-- src:34335 | made or caused to be made or proposes to make or to cause
-- src:34336 | to be made, or knows that a person associated with the
-- src:34337 | person has made or caused to be made or proposes to make
-- src:34338 | or to cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same
-- src:34339 | number, or substantially the same number, of the capital
-- src:34340 | markets products at a price that is substantially the same as
-- src:34341 | the firstmentioned price; or
@ref s 197(3)(b) (src:34333-34341)
GIVEN
    `the person makes or causes to be made an offer to sell the capital markets products at a specified price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person make, or cause to be made, an offer to sell the capital markets products at a specified price?
    `the person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person made or caused to be made, or does the person propose to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same number, or substantially the same number, of the capital markets products at a price that is substantially the same as the first-mentioned price?
    `the person knows that another person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person know that another person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same number, or substantially the same number, of the capital markets products at a price that is substantially the same as the first-mentioned price?
    `the other person is a person associated with the person (as section 3 reads)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person a person associated with the person? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 3(1), or NOTHING if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(3)(b) the person's purpose is presumed by reason of an offer to sell matched by an offer to purchase` MEANS
    IF `the person makes or causes to be made an offer to sell the capital markets products at a specified price` AND (`the person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` OR (`the person knows that another person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` AND (`the other person is a person associated with the person (as section 3 reads)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting subsection (1)"

