-- src:34355 | (4) The presumption under subsection (3) may be rebutted if the
-- src:34356 | defendant establishes that the purpose or purposes for which the
-- src:34357 | defendant did the act was not, or did not include, the purpose of
-- src:34358 | creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading in the
-- src:34359 | capital markets products on the organised market.
@ref s 197(4) (src:34355-34359)
GIVEN
    `the presumption under section 197(3) arises (the answer under section 197(3))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 197(3) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the defendant establishes that the purpose or purposes was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the defendant establish that the purpose or purposes for which the defendant did the act was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading in the capital markets products on the organised market?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(4) the presumption under subsection (3) is rebutted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the presumption under section 197(3) arises (the answer under section 197(3))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The presumption under subsection (3) may be rebutted"
        IF `the defendant establishes that the purpose or purposes was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be rebutted if the defendant establishes" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:34363 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a purchase or sale of capital
-- src:34364 | markets products does not involve a change in the beneficial
-- src:34365 | ownership if any of the following persons has an interest in the
-- src:34366 | capital markets products after the purchase or sale:
-- src:34371 | (a) a person who had an interest in the capital markets
-- src:34372 | products before the purchase or sale;
-- src:34374 | (b) a person associated with the person mentioned in
-- src:34375 | paragraph (a).
@ref s 197(5) (src:34363-34375)
GIVEN
    `a person who had an interest before the purchase or sale has an interest in the capital markets products after it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person who had an interest in the capital markets products before the purchase or sale have an interest in them after it?
    `a person has an interest in the capital markets products after the purchase or sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person have an interest in the capital markets products after the purchase or sale?
    `that person is associated with a person who had an interest before the purchase or sale (as section 3 reads)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is that person associated with a person who had an interest in the capital markets products before the purchase or sale? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 3(1), or NOTHING if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(5) the purchase or sale does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a person who had an interest before the purchase or sale has an interest in the capital markets products after it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a person has an interest in the capital markets products after the purchase or sale` AND (`that person is associated with a person who had an interest before the purchase or sale (as section 3 reads)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a person has an interest in the capital markets products after the purchase or sale` AND (`that person is associated with a person who had an interest before the purchase or sale (as section 3 reads)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is associated is not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership if any of the following persons has an interest" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:34379 | (6) In any proceedings against a person for a contravention of
-- src:34380 | subsection (2) in relation to a purchase or sale of capital markets
-- src:34381 | products that did not involve a change in the beneficial ownership of
-- src:34382 | the capital markets products, it is a defence if the defendant
-- src:34383 | establishes that the purpose or purposes for which the defendant
-- src:34384 | purchased or sold the capital markets products was not, or did not
-- src:34385 | include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance with
-- src:34386 | respect to the market for, or the price of, the capital markets products.
@ref s 197(6) (src:34379-34386)
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 197(2) in relation to a purchase or sale that did not involve a change in the beneficial ownership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for a contravention of section 197(2) in relation to a purchase or sale of capital markets products that did not involve a change in the beneficial ownership?
    `the defendant establishes that the purpose or purposes of the purchase or sale was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, the capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the defendant establish that the purpose or purposes for which the defendant purchased or sold the capital markets products was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, the capital markets products?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(6) the defendant has the defence to a contravention of subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 197(2) in relation to a purchase or sale that did not involve a change in the beneficial ownership`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings against a person for a contravention of subsection (2) in relation to a purchase or sale of capital markets products that did not involve a change in the beneficial ownership"
        IF `the defendant establishes that the purpose or purposes of the purchase or sale was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, the capital markets products`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence if the defendant establishes" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [DEFENCE]

-- src:34390 | (7) The reference in subsection (3)(a) to a transaction of purchase
-- src:34391 | or sale of the capital markets products includes —
-- src:34393 | (a) a reference to the making of an offer to purchase or sell the
-- src:34394 | capital markets products; and
-- src:34396 | (b) a reference to the making of an invitation, however
-- src:34397 | expressed, that expressly or impliedly invites a person to
-- src:34398 | offer to purchase or sell the capital markets products.
@ref s 197(7) (src:34390-34398)
GIVEN
    `the act is the making of an offer to purchase or sell the capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act the making of an offer to purchase or sell the capital markets products?
    `the act is the making of an invitation, however expressed, that expressly or impliedly invites a person to offer to purchase or sell the capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act the making of an invitation, however expressed, that expressly or impliedly invites a person to offer to purchase or sell the capital markets products?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(7) the act is within the reference to a transaction of purchase or sale in subsection (3)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the act is the making of an offer to purchase or sell the capital markets products` OR `the act is the making of an invitation, however expressed, that expressly or impliedly invites a person to offer to purchase or sell the capital markets products`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes"

§ `ss 197 to 203: the prohibitions as regulative rules`

-- Every prohibition of Division 1 is a SHANT over one act of its own. The party is "a person" (the Act names no narrower party),
-- here the core's Individual; a corporation or any other person is the same rule with another core Party.
-- A SHANT with no deadline stays open while nothing is done (RESIDUAL) and is BREACHed when the forbidden act is done.
DECLARE `s 197 to s 203 prohibited act` IS ONE OF
    `s 197(1) do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct for the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance`
    `s 197(1A) do a thing that creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance, knowingly or recklessly`
    `s 197(2) maintain, inflate, depress or cause fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products by a purchase or sale with no change in beneficial ownership, or by a fictitious transaction or device`
    `s 198(1) effect, take part in or carry out 2 or more transactions in securities of a corporation with the intent to induce others to subscribe for, purchase or sell`
    `s 198(2) effect, take part in or carry out 2 or more transactions in securities of a business trust with the intent to induce others to subscribe for, purchase or sell`
    `s 199 make a statement, or disseminate information, that is false or misleading in a material particular`
    `s 200(1) induce or attempt to induce another person to deal in capital markets products by a misleading, false or deceptive statement, a dishonest concealment, or false recorded information`
    `s 201 employ a device or practice to defraud, make a statement known to be false, or omit a material fact, in connection with the subscription, purchase or sale of capital markets products`
    `s 201A(1) knowingly execute, or hold out as executed, an order for a derivatives contract without having effected a purchase or sale in good faith`
    `s 201A(2) knowingly execute, or hold out as executed, an order for a spot foreign exchange contract without having effected a purchase or sale in good faith`
    `s 201B manipulate or attempt to manipulate the price of a derivatives contract or its underlying thing, or corner or attempt to corner an underlying thing`
    `s 202 circulate or disseminate a statement or information about the price effect of an illegal transaction`

§ `s 198: market manipulation in relation to securities and securities-based derivatives contracts`

-- src:34405 | 198.—(1) A person must not effect, take part in, be concerned in or
-- src:34406 | carry out, directly or indirectly, 2 or more transactions in securities, or
-- src:34407 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, of a corporation, being
-- src:34408 | transactions that have, or are likely to have, the effect of raising,
-- src:34409 | lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price of securities, or
-- src:34410 | securities‑based derivatives contracts (as the case may be) of the
-- src:34411 | corporation on an organised market, with the intent to induce other
-- src:34412 | persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities, or
-- src:34413 | securities‑based derivatives contracts (as the case may be) of the
-- src:34414 | corporation or of a related corporation.
@ref s 198(1) (src:34405-34414)
GIVEN
    `the number of transactions in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation that the person effected, took part in, was concerned in or carried out` IS A NUMBER @desc How many transactions in securities, or securities-based derivatives contracts, of the corporation did the person effect, take part in, be concerned in or carry out, directly or indirectly?
    `the transactions have, or are likely to have, the effect of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the transactions have, or are they likely to have, the effect of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts on an organised market?
    `the person acted with the intent to induce other persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or of a related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person act with the intent to induce other persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or of a related corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(1) the person's transactions contravene the bar on market manipulation in securities of a corporation` MEANS
    IF (`the number of transactions in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation that the person effected, took part in, was concerned in or carried out` AT LEAST 2) AND `the transactions have, or are likely to have, the effect of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price on an organised market` AND `the person acted with the intent to induce other persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or of a related corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "2 or more transactions in securities" "with the intent to induce other persons" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

@ref s 198(1) (src:34405-34414)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 to s 203 prohibited act`
`s 198(1) a person must not carry out 2 or more transactions in a corporation's securities with the intent to induce others to deal` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 198(1) effect, take part in or carry out 2 or more transactions in securities of a corporation with the intent to induce others to subscribe for, purchase or sell`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person carried out 2 or more transactions in securities of a corporation that affect the price, with the intent to induce others to subscribe for, purchase or sell (section 198(1))"

-- src:34421 | (2) A person must not effect, take part in, be concerned in or carry
-- src:34422 | out, directly or indirectly, 2 or more transactions in securities, or
-- src:34423 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, of a business trust, being
-- src:34424 | transactions that have, or are likely to have, the effect of raising,
-- src:34425 | lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price of securities, or
-- src:34426 | securities‑based derivatives contracts (as the case may be) of the
-- src:34427 | business trust on an organised market, with the intent to induce other
-- src:34428 | persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities, or
-- src:34429 | securities‑based derivatives contracts (as the case may be) of the
-- src:34430 | business trust.
@ref s 198(2) (src:34421-34430)
GIVEN
