@ref s 200(3) (src:34532-34543)
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 200(1) in relation to dealing in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceedings are for a contravention of section 200(1) in relation to dealing in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme?
    `the opinion is that of a public accountant as to the financial position of a company at a time or during a period for which the accountant made an audit or examination according to recognised audit practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the opinion is that of a public accountant as to the financial position of a company at a time or during a period for which the accountant made an audit or examination according to recognised audit practice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 200(3) the public accountant's opinion is admissible as evidence of the financial position of the company` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 200(1) in relation to dealing in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` AND `the opinion is that of a public accountant as to the financial position of a company at a time or during a period for which the accountant made an audit or examination according to recognised audit practice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is admissible, for any party to the proceedings, as evidence of the financial position of the company"

§ `s 201: employment of manipulative and deceptive devices`

-- src:34549 | 201. A person must not, directly or indirectly, in connection with
-- src:34550 | the subscription, purchase or sale of any capital markets products —
-- src:34552 | (a) employ any device, scheme or artifice to defraud;
-- src:34554 | (b) engage in any act, practice or course of business which
-- src:34555 | operates as a fraud or deception, or is likely to operate as a
-- src:34556 | fraud or deception, upon any person;
-- src:34558 | (c) make any statement the person knows to be false in a
-- src:34559 | material particular; or
-- src:34564 | (d) omit to state a material fact necessary in order to make the
-- src:34565 | statements made, in the light of the circumstances under
-- src:34566 | which they were made, not misleading.
@ref s 201 (src:34549-34566)
GIVEN
    `the person acts, directly or indirectly, in connection with the subscription, purchase or sale of capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person act, directly or indirectly, in connection with the subscription, purchase or sale of capital markets products?
    `the person employs a device, scheme or artifice to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person employs a device, scheme or artifice to defraud?
    `the person engages in an act, practice or course of business which operates as a fraud or deception, or is likely to do so, upon any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person engages in an act, practice or course of business which operates as a fraud or deception, or is likely to do so, upon any person?
    `the person makes a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person makes a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular?
    `the person omits to state a material fact necessary in order to make the statements made not misleading in the light of the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person omits to state a material fact necessary in order to make the statements made not misleading in the light of the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201 the person's conduct contravenes the bar on manipulative and deceptive devices` MEANS
    IF `the person acts, directly or indirectly, in connection with the subscription, purchase or sale of capital markets products` AND (`the person employs a device, scheme or artifice to defraud` OR `the person engages in an act, practice or course of business which operates as a fraud or deception, or is likely to do so, upon any person` OR `the person makes a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular` OR `the person omits to state a material fact necessary in order to make the statements made not misleading in the light of the circumstances`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with the subscription, purchase or sale of any capital markets products" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

@ref s 201 (src:34549-34566)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 to s 203 prohibited act`
`s 201 a person must not employ a manipulative or deceptive device in connection with a subscription, purchase or sale` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 201 employ a device or practice to defraud, make a statement known to be false, or omit a material fact, in connection with the subscription, purchase or sale of capital markets products`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person employed a device to defraud, engaged in a fraudulent practice, made a statement known to be false or omitted a material fact in connection with a subscription, purchase or sale (section 201)"

§ `s 201A: bucketing`

-- src:34572 | 201A.—(1) A person must not knowingly execute, or hold himself,
-- src:34573 | herself or itself out as having executed, an order for the purchase or
-- src:34574 | sale of a derivatives contract, without having effected in good faith a
-- src:34575 | purchase or sale of that derivatives contract in accordance with the
