§ `s 202: dissemination of information about illegal transactions`

-- src:34664 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), the condition is either —
-- src:34666 | (a) the person mentioned in subsection (1), or a person
-- src:34667 | associated with that person, has entered into or purports
-- src:34668 | to enter into any such transaction, or has done or purports
-- src:34669 | to do any such act or thing; or
-- src:34671 | (b) the person mentioned in subsection (1), or a person
-- src:34672 | associated with that person, has received, or expects to
-- src:34673 | receive, directly or indirectly, any consideration or benefit
-- src:34674 | for circulating or disseminating, or authorising or being
-- src:34675 | concerned in the circulation or dissemination of, the
-- src:34676 | statement or information.
@ref s 202(2) (src:34664-34676)
GIVEN
    `the person has entered into or purports to enter into the transaction, or has done or purports to do the act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into or purported to enter into any such transaction, or done or purported to do any such act or thing?
    `a person associated with the person has entered into or purports to enter into the transaction, or has done or purports to do the act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person associated with the person entered into or purported to enter into any such transaction, or done or purported to do any such act or thing?
    `the person has received, or expects to receive, directly or indirectly, a consideration or benefit for circulating or disseminating the statement or information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person received, or does the person expect to receive, directly or indirectly, any consideration or benefit for circulating or disseminating, or authorising or being concerned in the circulation or dissemination of, the statement or information?
    `a person associated with the person has received, or expects to receive, directly or indirectly, a consideration or benefit for the circulation or dissemination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person associated with the person received, or does such a person expect to receive, directly or indirectly, any consideration or benefit for circulating or disseminating, or authorising or being concerned in the circulation or dissemination of, the statement or information?
    `the associated person is associated with the person (as section 3 reads)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person associated with the person? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 3(1), or NOTHING if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(2) a condition in subsection (1) is satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has entered into or purports to enter into the transaction, or has done or purports to do the act or thing` OR `the person has received, or expects to receive, directly or indirectly, a consideration or benefit for circulating or disseminating the statement or information`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`a person associated with the person has entered into or purports to enter into the transaction, or has done or purports to do the act or thing` OR `a person associated with the person has received, or expects to receive, directly or indirectly, a consideration or benefit for the circulation or dissemination`) AND (`the associated person is associated with the person (as section 3 reads)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`a person associated with the person has entered into or purports to enter into the transaction, or has done or purports to do the act or thing` OR `a person associated with the person has received, or expects to receive, directly or indirectly, a consideration or benefit for the circulation or dissemination`) AND (`the associated person is associated with the person (as section 3 reads)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the other person is associated is not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the condition is either" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:34605 | 202.—(1) A person must not circulate or disseminate, or authorise
-- src:34606 | or be concerned in the circulation or dissemination of, any statement
-- src:34607 | or information to any of the following effect if any condition in
-- src:34608 | subsection (2) is satisfied:
