-- src:34652 | foreign exchange trading, by one or more persons which
-- src:34653 | to the person’s knowledge was entered into, or done, in
-- src:34654 | contravention of section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B, or if
-- src:34659 | entered into, or done, would be in contravention of
-- src:34660 | section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B.
@ref s 202(1) (src:34605-34660)
GIVEN
    `the person circulated or disseminated, or authorised or was concerned in the circulation or dissemination of, a statement or information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person circulate or disseminate, or authorise or be concerned in the circulation or dissemination of, a statement or information?
    `the statement or information is to the effect that the price of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 198, 199, 200 or 201` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement or information to the effect that the price of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or other act that, to the person's knowledge, was entered into or done in contravention of section 197, 198, 199, 200 or 201 (or would be if entered into or done)?
    `the statement or information is to the effect that the price of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 198, 199, 200 or 201` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement or information to the effect that the price of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or other act that, to the person's knowledge, was entered into or done in contravention of section 197, 198, 199, 200 or 201 (or would be if entered into or done)?
    `the statement or information is to the effect that the price of a class of derivatives contracts will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement or information to the effect that the price of a class of derivatives contracts will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or other act that, to the person's knowledge, was entered into or done in contravention of section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B (or would be if entered into or done)?
    `the statement or information is to the effect that the price of a class of spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement or information to the effect that the price of a class of spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or other act that, to the person's knowledge, was entered into or done in contravention of section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B (or would be if entered into or done)?
    `a condition in subsection (1) is satisfied (the answer under section 202(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 202(2) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(1) the person's circulation of a statement or information contravenes the bar on disseminating information about illegal transactions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person circulated or disseminated, or authorised or was concerned in the circulation or dissemination of, a statement or information` AND (`the statement or information is to the effect that the price of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 198, 199, 200 or 201` OR `the statement or information is to the effect that the price of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 198, 199, 200 or 201` OR `the statement or information is to the effect that the price of a class of derivatives contracts will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B` OR `the statement or information is to the effect that the price of a class of spot foreign exchange contracts for purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading will, or is likely to, rise or fall or be maintained by reason of a transaction or act that to the person's knowledge was in contravention of section 197, 200, 201, 201A or 201B`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any of the following effect" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `a condition in subsection (1) is satisfied (the answer under section 202(2))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a condition in subsection (1) is satisfied (the answer under section 202(2))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the condition in subsection (2) was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if any condition in subsection (2) is satisfied" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 202(1) (src:34605-34660)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 197 to s 203 prohibited act`
`s 202(1) a person must not circulate a statement or information about the price effect of an illegal transaction` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "a person"
    SHANT `s 202 circulate or disseminate a statement or information about the price effect of an illegal transaction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person circulated or disseminated a statement or information that a transaction known to contravene section 197, 198, 199, 200 or 201 will move a price, and a condition in section 202(2) was satisfied (section 202(1))"

§ `s 203: continuous disclosure`

-- src:34695 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to any of the following:
-- src:34697 | (a) an entity, the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:34698 | contracts of which are listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:34699 | exchange;
-- src:34701 | (b) a trustee‑manager of a business trust, where the securities
-- src:34702 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts of the business
-- src:34703 | trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange;
-- src:34708 | (c) a responsible person of a collective investment scheme,
-- src:34709 | where the units in the collective investment scheme are
-- src:34710 | listed for quotation on an approved exchange.
@ref s 203(2) (src:34695-34710)
GIVEN
    `the person is an entity the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of which are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of which are listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `the person is a trustee-manager of a business trust whose securities or securities-based derivatives contracts are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee-manager of a business trust, the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of which are listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `the person is a responsible person of a collective investment scheme whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a responsible person of a collective investment scheme, the units in which are listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(2) subsection (1) applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an entity the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of which are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` OR `the person is a trustee-manager of a business trust whose securities or securities-based derivatives contracts are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` OR `the person is a responsible person of a collective investment scheme whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Subsection (1) applies to any of the following"

-- src:34682 | 203.—(1) A person to whom this subsection applies must not
-- src:34683 | intentionally, recklessly or negligently fail to notify the approved
-- src:34684 | exchange of such information as is required to be disclosed by the
-- src:34685 | approved exchange under the listing rules or any other requirement of
-- src:34686 | the approved exchange, if the person is required by the approved
-- src:34687 | exchange under the listing rules or any other requirement of the
-- src:34688 | approved exchange to notify the approved exchange of information
-- src:34689 | on specified events or matters as they occur or arise for the purpose of
-- src:34690 | the approved exchange making that information available to an
-- src:34691 | organised market operated by the approved exchange.
@ref s 203(1) (src:34682-34691)
GIVEN
    `subsection (1) applies to the person (the answer under section 203(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 203(2) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the person is required by the approved exchange, under the listing rules or any other requirement, to notify it of information on specified events or matters as they occur or arise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person required by the approved exchange, under the listing rules or any other requirement of the approved exchange, to notify the approved exchange of information on specified events or matters as they occur or arise, for the purpose of the approved exchange making that information available to an organised market it operates?
    `the person failed to notify the approved exchange of the information required to be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person fail to notify the approved exchange of such information as is required to be disclosed by the approved exchange?
    `the failure was intentional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure to notify intentional?
    `the failure was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure to notify reckless?
    `the failure was negligent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure to notify negligent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(1) the person's failure to notify the approved exchange contravenes the bar on failing to disclose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (1) applies to the person (the answer under section 203(2))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (1) applies is not answered
        IF NOT (`subsection (1) applies to the person (the answer under section 203(2))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person to whom this subsection applies" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the person failed to notify the approved exchange of the information required to be disclosed` AND `the person is required by the approved exchange, under the listing rules or any other requirement, to notify it of information on specified events or matters as they occur or arise` AND (`the failure was intentional` OR `the failure was reckless` OR `the failure was negligent`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person is required by the approved exchange under the listing rules" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

-- Section 203(1) is a duty to notify. The Act sets no time of its own: the approved exchange's listing rules or requirement say when ("as they occur or arise"),
-- so the number of days is an input and the unit is days by this file's convention.
@ref s 203(1) (src:34682-34691)
GIVEN
    `the number of days within which the approved exchange requires the person to notify it` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days of the event or matter occurring or arising does the approved exchange require the person to notify it of the information?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 203 duty to notify`
`s 203(1) the person to whom subsection (1) applies must notify the approved exchange of the information it requires to be disclosed` MEANS
    PARTY `A corporation` "the person to whom section 203(1) applies"
    MUST `s 203(1) notify the approved exchange of the information required to be disclosed`
    WITHIN `the number of days within which the approved exchange requires the person to notify it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person did not notify the approved exchange of the information required to be disclosed within the time the approved exchange requires (section 203(1))"

-- src:34714 | (3) Despite section 204 or 335, a contravention of subsection (1) is
-- src:34715 | not an offence unless the failure to notify is intentional or reckless.
@ref s 203(3) (src:34714-34715)
GIVEN
    `the person's failure to notify contravenes subsection (1) (the answer under section 203(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 203(1) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the failure was intentional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure to notify intentional?
    `the failure was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure to notify reckless?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(3) the contravention of subsection (1) is an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person's failure to notify contravenes subsection (1) (the answer under section 203(1))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN `the person's failure to notify contravenes subsection (1) (the answer under section 203(1))`
        IF `the failure was intentional` OR `the failure was reckless`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not an offence unless the failure to notify is intentional or reckless"

DECLARE `s 203 duty to notify` IS ONE OF
    `s 203(1) notify the approved exchange of the information required to be disclosed`

§ `s 204: penalties under Division 1`

-- src:34721 | 204.—(1) Any person who contravenes any of the provisions of this
-- src:34722 | Division shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:34723 | to a fine not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:34724 | exceeding 7 years or to both.
@ref s 204(1) (src:34721-34724)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 204(1) the penalty on conviction for contravening a provision of Division 1` MEANS
    Penalty OF 250000, 84, TRUE, 0  -- fine not exceeding $250,000; imprisonment not exceeding 7 years (84 months); "or to both"; no daily fine stated

@ref s 204(1) (src:34721-34724)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a provision of Division 1 (the answer under the section that is contravened)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under the section of Division 1 that the person is said to contravene answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a provision of Division 1 (the answer under the section that is contravened)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any of the provisions of this Division" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

-- src:34726 | (2) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:34727 | offence in respect of a contravention of any of the provisions of this
-- src:34728 | Division after —
-- src:34730 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:34731 | payment of a civil penalty under section 232; or
-- src:34733 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:34734 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:34735 | civil penalty under section 232(5),
-- src:34737 | in respect of that contravention.
@ref s 204(2) (src:34726-34737)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention?
    `the person has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(2) proceedings for an offence in respect of the contravention are barred` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention` OR `the person has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence in respect of a contravention of any of the provisions of this Division after" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
